{"id":"mahabharata-7-027","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":27,"title":"सप्तविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 27 · Arjuna advances on Bhagadatta","summary":{"en":"Krishna drives Arjuna's swift horses toward Bhagadatta, and Arjuna scatters the Kaurava troops that block him. Bhagadatta then charges Arjuna on his elephant, crushing chariots and horses.","kn":"ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ವೇಗದ ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಭಗದತ್ತನತ್ತ ನಡೆಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಅಡ್ಡಬಂದ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಚದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭಗದತ್ತ ಆನೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ರಥ, ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ತುಳಿಯುತ್ತಾ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण अर्जुन के तेज़ घोड़ों को भगदत्त की ओर ले जाते हैं और अर्जुन रास्ता रोकने वाली कौरव सेना को बिखेर देते हैं। भगदत्त हाथी पर रथों और घोड़ों को कुचलते हुए अर्जुन पर चढ़ता है।","te":"కృష్ణుడు అర్జునుని వేగవంతమైన గుర్రాలను భగదత్తుని వైపు నడుపుతాడు; అర్జునుడు అడ్డుపడిన కౌరవ సేనను చెదరగొడతాడు. భగదత్తుడు ఏనుగుపై రథాలు గుర్రాలను తొక్కుతూ అర్జునునిపై దూసుకువస్తాడు.","ta":"கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனின் விரைவான குதிரைகளைப் பகதத்தனை நோக்கிச் செலுத்த, அர்ஜுனன் தடுக்கும் கௌரவப் படையைச் சிதறடிக்கிறான். பகதத்தன் யானைமேல் தேர்களையும் குதிரைகளையும் மிதித்தபடி அர்ஜுனனைத் தாக்குகிறான்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനന്റെ വേഗമുള്ള കുതിരകളെ ഭഗദത്തന്റെ നേർക്ക് തെളിക്കുന്നു; തടസ്സമായ കൗരവ സൈന്യത്തെ അർജുനൻ ചിതറിക്കുന്നു. പിന്നീട് ഭഗദത്തൻ ആനപ്പുറത്ത് അർജുനനെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; രഥങ്ങളെയും കുതിരകളെയും ഞെരിച്ചുകൊണ്ട്."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.27; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"संशप्तकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Samshaptakavadha Parva (Slaying of the Samshaptakas)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यियासतस्ततः कृष्णः पार्थस्याश्वान्मनोजवान् ।\nअप्रैषीद्धेमसंछन्नान्द्रोणानीकाय पाण्डुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Partha wished to go, Krishna drove his swift-as-thought white horses, covered in gold, toward Drona's division."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं प्रयान्तं कुरुश्रेष्ठं स्वांस्त्रातुं द्रोणतापितान् ।\nसुशर्मा भ्रातृभिः सार्धं युद्धार्थी पृष्ठतोऽन्वयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that best of the Kurus went to protect his own men tormented by Drona, Susharman followed from behind with his brothers, wanting to fight."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः श्वेतहयः कृष्णमब्रवीदजितं जयः ।\nएष मां भ्रातृभिः सार्धं सुशर्माह्वयतेऽच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Jaya, with white horses, said to the unconquerable Krishna: \"Achyuta, here is Susharman with his brothers challenging me.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"दीर्यते चोत्तरेणैतत्सैन्यं नः शत्रुसूदन ।\nद्वैधीभूतं मनो मेऽद्य कृतं संशप्तकैरिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Slayer of foes, our army is being torn apart to the north, and the Samshaptakas have today split my mind in two.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"किं नु संशप्तकान्हन्मि स्वान्रक्षाम्यहितार्दितान् ।\nइति मे त्वं मतं वेत्थ तत्र किं सुकृतं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Shall I kill the Samshaptakas, or protect my own men afflicted by enemies? You know my mind; what would be right in this?\""}},{"n":6,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु दाशार्हः स्यन्दनं प्रत्यवर्तयत् ।\nयेन त्रिगर्ताधिपतिः पाण्डवं समुपाह्वयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, the Dasharha turned the chariot back, toward where the lord of the Trigartas was challenging the Pandava."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनः सुशर्माणं विद्ध्वा सप्तभिराशुगैः ।\nध्वजं धनुश्चास्य तथा क्षुराभ्यां समकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna pierced Susharman with seven swift arrows and cut down his banner and bow with two razor-arrows."}},{"n":8,"text":"त्रिगर्ताधिपतेश्चापि भ्रातरं षड्भिरायसैः ।\nसाश्वं ससूतं त्वरितः पार्थः प्रैषीद्यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha quickly sent the Trigarta king's brother, with his horses and charioteer, to Yama's abode with six iron arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो भुजगसंकाशां सुशर्मा शक्तिमायसीम् ।\nचिक्षेपार्जुनमादिश्य वासुदेवाय तोमरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Susharman hurled an iron spear like a serpent at Arjuna, and a lance at Vasudeva."}},{"n":10,"text":"शक्तिं त्रिभिः शरैश्छित्त्वा तोमरं त्रिभिरर्जुनः ।\nसुशर्माणं शरव्रातैर्मोहयित्वा न्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna cut down the spear with three arrows and the lance with three, bewildered Susharman with swarms of arrows, and turned away."}},{"n":11,"text":"तं वासवमिवायान्तं भूरिवर्षशरौघिणम् ।\nराजंस्तावकसैन्यानां नोग्रं कश्चिदवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, no one among your armies could stop him as he came like Indra, fierce, pouring a mighty flood of arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो धनंजयो बाणैस्तत एव महारथान् ।\nआयाद्विनिघ्नन्कौरव्यान्दहन्कक्षमिवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dhananjaya went at those great warriors with his arrows, killing Kauravas and burning them like a fire burning dry grass."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्य वेगमसह्यं तु कुन्तीपुत्रस्य धीमतः ।\nनाशक्नुवंस्ते संसोढुं स्पर्शमग्नेरिव प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men could not endure the unbearable force of the wise son of Kunti, as creatures cannot bear the touch of fire."}},{"n":14,"text":"संवेष्टयन्ननीकानि शरवर्षेण पाण्डवः ।\nसुपर्णपातवद्राजन्नायात्प्राग्ज्योतिषं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enveloping the armies in showers of arrows, the Pandava, O king, went toward Pragjyotisha like a falling eagle."}},{"n":15,"text":"यत्तदानामयज्जिष्णुर्भरतानामपायिनाम् ।\nधनुः क्षेमकरं संख्ये द्विषतामश्रुवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jishnu bent the bow that had brought safety to the Bharatas in battle and increased the tears of enemies,"}},{"n":16,"text":"तदेव तव पुत्रस्य राजन्दुर्द्यूतदेविनः ।\nकृते क्षत्रविनाशाय धनुरायच्छदर्जुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and, O king, that same bow Arjuna now drew for the destruction of the Kshatriyas, for the sake of your son, who gambled falsely."}},{"n":17,"text":"तथा विक्षोभ्यमाणा सा पार्थेन तव वाहिनी ।\nव्यदीर्यत महाराज नौरिवासाद्य पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So agitated by Partha, your army was torn apart, O great king, like a ship striking a mountain."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो दश सहस्राणि न्यवर्तन्त धनुष्मताम् ।\nमतिं कृत्वा रणे क्रुद्धा वीरा जयपराजये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then ten thousand archers turned back, angry heroes, resolved in battle on victory or defeat."}},{"n":19,"text":"व्यपेतहृदयत्रास आपद्धर्मातिगो रथः ।\nआर्छत्पार्थो गुरुं भारं सर्वभारसहो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fearless in heart, never breaking the rules even in danger, Partha's chariot took on a heavy burden, bearing every burden in the war."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथा नडवनं क्रुद्धः प्रभिन्नः षष्टिहायनः ।\nमृद्नीयात्तद्वदायस्तः पार्थोऽमृद्नाच्चमूं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As an angry sixty-year-old rutting elephant tramples a reed-bed, so the exerted Partha trampled your army."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्मिन्प्रमथिते सैन्ये भगदत्तो नराधिपः ।\nतेन नागेन सहसा धनंजयमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that army was being crushed, King Bhagadatta suddenly charged at Dhananjaya with that same elephant."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं रथेन नरव्याघ्रः प्रत्यगृह्णादभीतवत् ।\nस संनिपातस्तुमुलो बभूव रथनागयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tiger among men met him fearlessly in his chariot, and the clash of chariot and elephant was tumultuous."}},{"n":23,"text":"कल्पिताभ्यां यथाशास्त्रं रथेन च गजेन च ।\nसंग्रामे चेरतुर्वीरौ भगदत्तधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhagadatta and Dhananjaya, two heroes, one with chariot and one with elephant, both properly prepared by the rules, moved about in the battle."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततो जीमूतसंकाशान्नागादिन्द्र इवाभिभूः ।\nअभ्यवर्षच्छरौघेण भगदत्तो धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhagadatta, like Indra overpowering from a cloud-like elephant, showered Dhananjaya with a flood of arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"स चापि शरवर्षं तच्छरवर्षेण वासविः ।\nअप्राप्तमेव चिच्छेद भगदत्तस्य वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the mighty son of Indra, Arjuna, cut down that rain of arrows with his own rain of arrows before it reached him."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः प्राग्ज्योतिषो राजा शरवर्षं निवार्य तत् ।\nशरैर्जघ्ने महाबाहुं पार्थं कृष्णं च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Pragjyotisha, warding off that rain of arrows, struck the mighty-armed Partha and Krishna with arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः स शरजालेन महताभ्यवकीर्य तौ ।\nचोदयामास तं नागं वधायाच्युतपार्थयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covering the two with a great net of arrows, he urged his elephant on to kill Achyuta and Partha."}},{"n":28,"text":"तमापतन्तं द्विरदं दृष्ट्वा क्रुद्धमिवान्तकम् ।\nचक्रेऽपसव्यं त्वरितः स्यन्दनेन जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that elephant charging like angry Death, Janardana quickly turned the chariot to the left."}},{"n":29,"text":"संप्राप्तमपि नेयेष परावृत्तं महाद्विपम् ।\nसारोहं मृत्युसात्कर्तुं स्मरन्धर्मं धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though the great elephant, turned away, came within reach, Dhananjaya, remembering dharma, did not wish to give it with its rider to death."}},{"n":30,"text":"स तु नागो द्विपरथान्हयांश्चारुज्य मारिष ।\nप्राहिणोन्मृत्युलोकाय ततोऽक्रुध्यद्धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That elephant crushed chariots, elephants and horses, O sir, and sent them to the world of death; then Dhananjaya grew angry."}}]}]}